                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e435999c-efe0-3c80-a882-89f23f1ac037",
                        "entry_id": "1251be4b-bdbc-33c3-8387-bc6b8467b355",
                        "glosses": [
                            "специалист по арифметике"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ae761b0-20d8-4d39-a1b3-83aa3af63a25",
                                "sense_id": "e435999c-efe0-3c80-a882-89f23f1ac037",
                                "text": "Приятность за приятностью и поцелуй за поцелуем следовали, сестра моя прижимала меня к сердцу и целовала весьма часто в груди, а я ей отвечала такою же благодарностию; словом, всех наших поцелуев никакой бы исправный арифметик исчислить не мог без ошибки."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5f6657b2-1a12-3365-b0ea-17175eeb4e15",
                        "entry_id": "1251be4b-bdbc-33c3-8387-bc6b8467b355",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. учитель арифметики"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2bff79a7-d6e2-4482-ad96-073b7fc78cef",
                        "source_entry_id": "1251be4b-bdbc-33c3-8387-bc6b8467b355",
                        "target_lang_word": "arithmetician",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "arithmetician",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8d93532-15a1-367f-ba89-f30b10e683b6",
                                        "entry_id": "8e54878f-a963-3211-a217-91693ae9259d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One with expertise in arithmetic; a mathematician."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "855f975a-ec18-4f55-a917-785dfb0e8e8e",
                                                "sense_id": "c8d93532-15a1-367f-ba89-f30b10e683b6",
                                                "text": "[F]or certes, ſayes he, / I haue already choſen my officer, and what was he? / Forſooth, a great Arithmeticion, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c55411b6-f2d3-4d3b-a3d2-08d546dd89ef",
                                                "sense_id": "c8d93532-15a1-367f-ba89-f30b10e683b6",
                                                "text": "I haue read the truest computer of Times, and the best Arithmetician that euer breathed, and he reduceth thy dayes into a short number: The daies of Man are threescore and ten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "102dac81-e6e8-462d-87b8-78bfd28ef88a",
                                                "sense_id": "c8d93532-15a1-367f-ba89-f30b10e683b6",
                                                "text": "But I'll tell you one thing; it's a Question that would puzzle an Arithmetician, if you ſhould ask him, whether the Bible ſaves more Souls in Weſtminſter-Abby, or damns more in Weſtminſter-Hall: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53538370-97ff-4c3f-9f6c-d1ccb1ea54c9",
                                                "sense_id": "c8d93532-15a1-367f-ba89-f30b10e683b6",
                                                "text": "Bonoro. What said he? / Tycho. That he would say but three words and follow me. I heard him say a hundred, and sing a thousand: Lovers are bad arithmeticians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87bb967f-82d6-4a06-a8b3-f72071d6ff5e",
                                                "sense_id": "c8d93532-15a1-367f-ba89-f30b10e683b6",
                                                "text": "You talk of figures, now; you have only to say to Stelling, ‘I want my son to be a thorough arithmetician,’ and you may leave the rest to him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
